pi-mcp-adapter — vendored bundled extension
============================================

Upstream package : pi-mcp-adapter 5.0.0 (MIT)
Upstream author  : Nico Bailon (https://github.com/nicobailon/pi-mcp-adapter)
License          : MIT — see LICENSE (copied verbatim from upstream)

This directory is OMA's bundled copy of the pi-mcp-adapter extension:

  upstream/        exact npm tarball content of pi-mcp-adapter@5.0.0,
                   unmodified — the integrity-pinned source snapshot. Every
                   tarball member — all 87 root .ts modules, dist/, docs/,
                   skills/, examples/, cli.js, the .cjs/.mjs helper assets,
                   LICENSE, README.md, CHANGELOG.md and package.json —
                   matches the source commit named in manifest.json
                   byte-for-byte (the tarball and the commit tree differ
                   only in files npm never ships: the test suites, configs,
                   .github and examples/interactive-visualizer).
  upstream-tests/  the upstream test tree from the source commit named in
                   manifest.json (the npm tarball ships no tests):
                   __tests__/, the root *.test.ts/*.test.mjs suites,
                   conformance/, test-runner.mjs, vitest.config.ts and the
                   tsconfigs — vendored for provenance and porting. Not
                   wired into npm test wholesale — upstream's suite needs
                   vitest, the upstream repo layout and for most suites a
                   network.
  node_modules/    the pinned runtime dependency closure — the resolved
                   production install of upstream's declared dependencies
                   (@modelcontextprotocol/client, @typesafe-ai/sdk, undici,
                   zod, jose, open, eventsource, quickjs-wasi, recheck,
                   @napi-rs/keyring and their transitive deps), byte-exact
                   to the npm-installed tree at vendoring time and named
                   with lockfile integrity in manifest.json — kept separate
                   from anything a user-installed Pi package would resolve.
                   npm's .bin symlink farm is not vendored (the bundle
                   forbids non-regular files, and nothing here runs the
                   bins). The platform-bound optional natives npm resolved
                   for linux-x64 are vendored as resolved
                   (@napi-rs/keyring-linux-x64-gnu, recheck-linux-x64);
                   under OMA the keyring store is closed by policy before
                   any native module is required, and recheck keeps its own
                   fallback order — the closure covers every path OMA can
                   reach. Peer/host API packages (@earendil-works/
                   pi-coding-agent, @earendil-works/pi-tui,
                   @earendil-works/pi-ai, typebox) are NOT vendored: they
                   resolve to OMA's own install.
  runtime/         compiled JavaScript + declarations of upstream's .ts
                   modules, generated by scripts/vendor-pi-mcp-adapter.mjs:
                   relative ".ts" specifiers are rewritten to ".js" before
                   tsc emit (Node's loader needs them), then OMA's declared
                   divergence splices are applied — the omaMcpPolicy seam
                   in utils.js (deny-by-default permits, the ambient-env
                   view, the OMA-owned agent dir and spill root, the
                   child-env scrub hook, the credential-store pin, the
                   OS-keyring closure) and the egress pin leaf carried by
                   the vendored undici (server-manager fetch chains,
                   mcp-auth-fetch, mcp-probe, jev-client), plus the
                   verbatim non-.ts payload (mcp-script-worker.mjs,
                   mcp-keyring-helper.cjs, app-bridge.bundle.js,
                   package.json, skills/). Generated, hash-pinned input —
                   not authored OMA code. Every upstream module is emitted;
                   OMA's adapter (src/extension/mcp-tools.ts) verifies the
                   bundle, installs the policy, then drives upstream's own
                   createMcpAdapter factory through a facade that admits
                   only the `mcp` tool registration.
  manifest.json    generated bundle manifest: per-file SHA-256, byte
                   counts and a deterministic whole-bundle digest, plus
                   the upstream name/version/commit, npm tarball
                   integrity/shasum metadata and the pinned dependency
                   closure.

No part of this bundle is fetched, installed or cloned at run time.
